course: dictionary
lesson: 14607
title: Pollutants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pollutant is a substance that makes air, water or soil dirty and harmful to living things. The word comes from pollute, which means to make something dirty or unsafe. «Smoke from the factory chimney is a pollutant that dirties the air.» The clue is in the words dirties and harmful: smoke is not just grey, it can hurt people who breathe it.
explain: Pollutants can come from many places. «Cars give out exhaust gas, and exhaust gas is a pollutant.» Other pollutants include plastic, oil, sewage and pesticides. Ask yourself: does this substance make the air, water or soil dirty, and can it harm living things? If yes, it is a pollutant.
explain: Pollutants harm more than one thing at once. «The oil leaked into the river, and the fish were harmed by the pollutant.» Oil in the river can hurt fish, birds and the people who live near the water. Scientists and geographers study pollutants to see how they damage health, rivers and wildlife.
explain: You can help reduce pollutants. Walking or cycling to school means fewer exhaust gases in the air. Recycling means less plastic ends up in the land and sea. Small choices, made by many people, can make a real difference.
fact: A pollutant is a substance that makes air, water or soil dirty and harmful.
fact: Car exhaust gases, smoke, plastic, oil, sewage and pesticides are all examples of pollutants.
fact: Pollutants can harm people's health, rivers and wildlife.
fact: Walking to school and recycling are two ways to reduce pollutants.
fact: «Pollutant» comes from the word pollute, which means to make something dirty or unsafe.
exercise: What is a pollutant? | *A substance that makes air, water or soil dirty and harmful to living things | A tasty food that is good for you | A type of bird that lives near rivers | A small plant that grows in shade
exercise: «The oil leaked into the river, and the fish were harmed by the pollutant.» What is the pollutant in this sentence? | Sunshine | Fish | Bridge | *Oil
exercise: Which of these is a pollutant? | *Car exhaust gas | Clean sand on a beach | Fresh air in the park | Rain water from the sky
test: Why do pollutants matter? | Because they are only found in shops | *Because they can harm people, rivers and wildlife | Because they help plants grow faster | Because they make the sky brighter and warmer
test: Which action helps to reduce pollutants? | Leaving the tap running | Burning rubbish in the garden | Dropping litter in the park | *Walking to school instead of being driven
exam: A friend says, «Plastic in the sea is a pollutant.» What does your friend mean? | Plastic is good for the sea and helps animals | Plastic is a kind of fish that lives in the sea | Plastic can be eaten by people safely | *Plastic makes the sea dirty and can harm living things
